": "Opus 5.5 pushed out with D5, which lost 3.2 points and took Black from -2.5 to -5.6. The engine preferred C7. White's stones at B5, B6 and C6 on the left were left firmly in place."}, {"turn": 20, "text": "White's E9 lost 5.7 points and swung the lead from +0.1 to +5.8 for Black. The engine wanted F2. Opus 5.5 had earned the lead with the E8 stone just before, a move the engine also chose."}, {"turn": 23, "text": "The decisive blunder. With Black ahead at +6.4, D1 lost 11.5 points and left Black at -5.0. The engine's choice was F8, on the upper side, where White's next move went anyway. A comfortable lead disappeared in one move."}, {"turn": 42, "text": "White's J6 was the 8k's worst move, losing 8.4 points, and the engine preferred B1. It moved the lead from -12.8 to -4.4 for Black, the one real chance to get back into the game."}, {"turn": 43, "text": "Opus 5.5 answered with G6, which lost 6.2 points, and the lead fell from -4.4 to -10.6. The engine's choice was B2. The chance created by White's slip was gone straight away."}, {"turn": 55, "text": "G3 lost 20.3 points, dropping Black from -7.6 to -27.9. The engine's choice was F2. White's E3 followed, and by the end White had stones at E3 and F3 beside Black's thin group at E2 and F2. Opus 5.5 resigned soon after."}]}, "audit": null}